<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#corvus">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Corvus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The corvus was a boarding bridge with a spike at its end, used by the Roman navy during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-punic-war">First Punic War</a>. It allowed Roman soldiers to board and fight on Carthaginian ships as if on land. The device helped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> overcome the superior seamanship of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>'s navy.</p></div>
